WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.320 --> 00:00:07.040
For more than a hundred thousand years, humanity
has buried their dead. We commit the bodies

00:00:07.040 --> 00:00:14.509
of our deceased to the ground, earth to earth,
ashes to ashes, dust to dust, in the hope

00:00:14.509 --> 00:00:20.869
that one day our dearly departed might get
to enjoy some form of eternal life. But eternal

00:00:20.869 --> 00:00:26.750
life might be less appealing than it sounds.
Perhaps there’s a reason that humans bury

00:00:26.750 --> 00:00:31.849
their dead… maybe it’s so that the dead
stay buried. And luckily, they do… At least,

00:00:31.849 --> 00:00:37.000
most of the time.
Accessible only via a cargo elevator, and

00:00:37.000 --> 00:00:42.250
not marked on any official Foundation blueprints,
beneath the northwest corner of Overwatch

00:00:42.250 --> 00:00:50.500
Command lies SCP-5555. This SCP isn’t a
creature or carnivorous monster, it’s not

00:00:50.500 --> 00:00:55.930
a gateway to another dimension or an entity
with the power to rewrite the very fabric

00:00:55.930 --> 00:01:04.199
of reality itself. No, SCP-5555 is a mass
grave filled with corpses. A pit of unknown

00:01:04.199 --> 00:01:11.170
origin and indeterminable depth, each body
exhumed from within SCP-5555 shows various

00:01:11.170 --> 00:01:16.820
anomalous traits. These bodies can be removed
from the mass grave without any incident,

00:01:16.820 --> 00:01:22.080
but given the incalculable depth of this vast,
corpse-filled pit, continued excavation of

00:01:22.080 --> 00:01:29.520
SCP-5555 would likely only reveal further
bodies, and fewer answers as to how they came

00:01:29.520 --> 00:01:33.240
to be buried beneath the Foundation’s Overwatch
Command.

00:01:33.240 --> 00:01:40.009
The bodies recovered during the initial excavation
of SCP-5555 vary in their physical attributes

00:01:40.009 --> 00:01:45.729
as well as their causes of death, when one
can even be determined. One body appears to

00:01:45.729 --> 00:01:52.250
be a man whose age and ethnicity are both
unclear, as is how he died. But his body is

00:01:52.250 --> 00:01:58.840
perfectly preserved, showing no signs of decomposition.
Another of the corpses, has its head covered

00:01:58.840 --> 00:02:04.340
with a burlap sack and a noose tightened around
its neck. When these are removed they reveal

00:02:04.340 --> 00:02:10.480
an identical noose and sack underneath. When
those are removed they reveal another. And

00:02:10.480 --> 00:02:18.440
on and on. The cause of death, in this instance,
is at least apparent - strangulation. Suggesting

00:02:18.440 --> 00:02:22.360
the deceased was intended to suffer before
their death.

00:02:22.360 --> 00:02:26.530
Some of the other bodies removed from the
pit include one belonging to a middle-aged

00:02:26.530 --> 00:02:32.210
Alutiiq woman, whose entire skeleton is formed
of ice that doesn’t melt under increased

00:02:32.210 --> 00:02:36.430
temperatures, while a different body is a
human male with eighty percent of its organs

00:02:36.430 --> 00:02:41.830
surgically replaced with artificial ones,
driven by gears and mechanisms that continue

00:02:41.830 --> 00:02:47.870
to tick away long after death. An adolescent
female with dark blue skin has two severed

00:02:47.870 --> 00:02:53.330
hands grasping its throat, while a Caucasian
woman was found with both of her eyes gouged

00:02:53.330 --> 00:02:57.070
out.
Perhaps most curious of all is the coffin,

00:02:57.070 --> 00:03:03.310
crafted from black stone, that cannot be opened.
All attempts to open it have been resisted

00:03:03.310 --> 00:03:08.420
by some form of internal force keeping the
coffin shut. While it’s unable to be opened,

00:03:08.420 --> 00:03:14.531
it is believed to contain a human inside.
A coffin with a person inside of it. Those

00:03:14.531 --> 00:03:20.050
familiar with the objects contained by the
Foundation may make a connection to SCP-076,

00:03:20.050 --> 00:03:28.600
Able, a humanoid entity also contained inside
a coffin. A curious connection too. As you’ll

00:03:28.600 --> 00:03:35.810
come to see, when dealing with SCP-5555, the
appearance of many familiar faces may be more

00:03:35.810 --> 00:03:41.230
than just vague connections.
None of these corpses, or their various anomalous

00:03:41.230 --> 00:03:49.160
properties, answer any of the pressing questions
about SCP-5555’s exact nature and origin.

00:03:49.160 --> 00:03:54.100
In fact, the bodies found within the grave
only raise new questions about this seemingly

00:03:54.100 --> 00:04:00.070
bottomless pit that the Foundation was either
built over, or knowingly hides beneath its

00:04:00.070 --> 00:04:06.720
lowest depths.
The truth behind SCP-5555 is shrouded in mystery,

00:04:06.720 --> 00:04:12.040
unanswered questions piled on top of each
other like the bodies in the mass grave itself,

00:04:12.040 --> 00:04:18.239
a pile that stacks all the way up to the highest
levels of the Foundation’s own administration.

00:04:18.239 --> 00:04:25.780
In actuality, the bodies buried in SCP-5555
are part of a vast and insidious game, played

00:04:25.780 --> 00:04:32.250
by the heads of a number of GOIs, or Groups
of Interest, as well as the SCP Foundation’s

00:04:32.250 --> 00:04:37.930
very own Administrator. But how do the corpses
of these anomalous beings factor into the

00:04:37.930 --> 00:04:45.910
aforementioned game, and what is its ultimate
outcome? Examining the file describing SCP-5555,

00:04:45.910 --> 00:04:51.340
albeit with adequate O5 security clearance,
answers some of those burning questions about

00:04:51.340 --> 00:04:55.930
the mystery at play.
Dr. Everett Mann, the current O5-1, was the

00:04:55.930 --> 00:05:02.530
first to uncover the existence of SCP-5555
and the corpses contained within it. Mann

00:05:02.530 --> 00:05:08.370
created a series of notes detailing his findings,
intended for his successor. In these, Mann

00:05:08.370 --> 00:05:13.400
claimed that the Administrator, one Francis
Fritzwilliams, the only figure with authority

00:05:13.400 --> 00:05:19.190
above that of the O5 Council, blackballed
him - meaning Fritzwilliams had voted against

00:05:19.190 --> 00:05:23.910
allowing Dr. Mann to remain a member of the
SCP Foundation.

00:05:23.910 --> 00:05:28.900
Everett Mann had believed the Administrator
to be his friend, so naturally it came as

00:05:28.900 --> 00:05:33.930
a surprise when ‘Fritz’ framed him for
an elaborate plot to eliminate Mann’s fellow

00:05:33.930 --> 00:05:40.030
Overseer Council members. Based on information
from his own O5-1 predecessor, Mann believed

00:05:40.030 --> 00:05:44.840
whoever took up the role after he was voted
out would have to take up the role of killing

00:05:44.840 --> 00:05:50.260
Fritz for the good of the Foundation. But
what connection between Fritz and a pit full

00:05:50.260 --> 00:05:55.260
of anomalous corpses could possibly warrant
Mann urging his successor to eliminate the

00:05:55.260 --> 00:05:59.880
Foundation’s Administrator?
Dr Mann’s notes to his successor continue

00:05:59.880 --> 00:06:04.770
with detailed instructions as to how they
would go about killing Fritz, and that firstly,

00:06:04.770 --> 00:06:10.080
they would require a lair. Mann himself was
holed up in an isolated Arctic shack for three

00:06:10.080 --> 00:06:15.450
decades after being blackballed by the Administrator,
before Fritz sent his own private death squad

00:06:15.450 --> 00:06:20.860
after the former Overseer. Mann stressed the
importance of having a defensible, isolated

00:06:20.860 --> 00:06:26.730
location, stocked with armed guards and traps
for his successor to lie in wait for Fritz.

00:06:26.730 --> 00:06:31.760
It was because of the traps Mann had set in
his shack that he was able to escape Fritz’s

00:06:31.760 --> 00:06:37.180
death squad with his life.
Secondly, Mann urges his new O5-1 successor

00:06:37.180 --> 00:06:43.000
to always have several escape plans in place,
and to be prepared to leave the lair, or indeed

00:06:43.000 --> 00:06:48.750
any other location, at any time. Dr. Mann
also suggested telling falsified escape plans

00:06:48.750 --> 00:06:54.350
to close friends, in case Fritz got to them
first, or finding an SCP that allows the new

00:06:54.350 --> 00:07:01.290
O5-1 to teleport to safety. Third, Mann suggests
the need for multiple, fully-stocked safehouses.

00:07:01.290 --> 00:07:06.770
After all, escape plans are entirely pointless
unless you’ve got somewhere secure to actually

00:07:06.770 --> 00:07:10.340
escape to.
Everett Mann also suggested, much like his

00:07:10.340 --> 00:07:16.480
advice with escape plans, to have fake safehouses
or SCP anomalies on-hand to get you to the

00:07:16.480 --> 00:07:23.480
real ones. How does one obtain access to an
SCP? According to Mann, placing moles or blackmailing

00:07:23.480 --> 00:07:28.860
personnel within every Foundation facility
is one way, as doing so granted him access

00:07:28.860 --> 00:07:36.580
to SCP-268, a hat that makes its wearer practically
invisible, which came in handy during his

00:07:36.580 --> 00:07:39.250
escape.
Of course, installing your own trusted moles

00:07:39.250 --> 00:07:44.889
is a potentially tricky feat to accomplish,
given that Fritz has the entire Foundation,

00:07:44.889 --> 00:07:50.330
and many other Groups of Interest in his thrall.
But if anyone has the power to do so, and

00:07:50.330 --> 00:07:55.940
by extension the power to bring Fitz down,
it would be another Overseer.

00:07:55.940 --> 00:07:59.920
Of course, Mann’s plot to eliminate Fritz
and highly-detailed words of warning to his

00:07:59.920 --> 00:08:05.000
successor do little to explain the pit full
of anomalous corpses. Contained within the

00:08:05.000 --> 00:08:13.080
file for SCP-5555 is an email to the Foundation’s
Administrator from the CEO of Wondertainment,

00:08:13.080 --> 00:08:18.550
an anomalous toy manufacturer and one of a
number of Groups of Interest to the Foundation.

00:08:18.550 --> 00:08:25.080
In it, the CEO congratulates Fritz on an excellent
win, and asks for a copy of an unknown file,

00:08:25.080 --> 00:08:28.920
as well as mentioning the leaders of other
Groups of Interest such as the Church of the

00:08:28.920 --> 00:08:34.700
Broken God. According to the email, this unidentified
file was to be sent physically as opposed

00:08:34.700 --> 00:08:42.659
to electronically, giving Dr Mann his next
lead in uncovering the mystery of SCP-5555.

00:08:42.659 --> 00:08:48.020
Mann traveled to the headquarters of Wondertainment,
‘Wonderworld’, to retrieve the file, using

00:08:48.020 --> 00:08:53.880
his special hat to avoid detection. Seems
like an easy enough task, except Wonderworld

00:08:53.880 --> 00:09:00.650
is a pocket dimension that slowly transforms
human beings into…something else. Time working

00:09:00.650 --> 00:09:05.200
against him, Mann hastily made his way to
Wonder Tower, and attempted to recover the

00:09:05.200 --> 00:09:10.700
file that would maybe give him all the answers
to this bizarre, twisted mystery. Unfortunately,

00:09:10.700 --> 00:09:15.900
Wondertainment’s CEO, Dr. Holly Wondertainment,
got to him first.

00:09:15.900 --> 00:09:20.690
Confronted by Dr. Wondertainment, Everett
Mann demanded to know who was involved in

00:09:20.690 --> 00:09:26.420
the scheme, besides her and the Administrator.
He posited that the O5 Council might be somehow

00:09:26.420 --> 00:09:30.830
involved, but Dr. Wondertainment claimed that
the game being played was above and beyond

00:09:30.830 --> 00:09:35.770
their little ‘numbers club’. Holly proceeded
to point a large, acid-filled Super Soaker

00:09:35.770 --> 00:09:41.080
at Mann, and ordered him down onto his knees
when he asked what the purpose of the mass

00:09:41.080 --> 00:09:47.490
grave, SCP-5555, was.
Following a fight and the apparent death of

00:09:47.490 --> 00:09:52.980
Dr Wondertainment, Mann escaped Wonderworld
with the file, containing an updated version

00:09:52.980 --> 00:09:57.880
of the SCP-5555 description and containment
procedures.

00:09:57.880 --> 00:10:04.830
The key points featured in this SCP-5555 document
are mentions of sealing the mass grave with

00:10:04.830 --> 00:10:11.010
concrete after completing the ‘turnover’
and re-establishing ‘the façade’. It

00:10:11.010 --> 00:10:17.170
also mentions that any already-catalogued
SCP entering the pit will die, with its personality,

00:10:17.170 --> 00:10:22.430
attributes and any anomalous qualities being
passed on to a new entity, which will appear

00:10:22.430 --> 00:10:28.280
close to the location of the initial SCP’s
discovery. So, the pit can not only kill any

00:10:28.280 --> 00:10:34.690
SCP that enters it, but can also instantly
recreate them with slight differences and

00:10:34.690 --> 00:10:42.040
reposition them. Does this mean the bodies
in SCP-5555 are those of former SCPs? To answer

00:10:42.040 --> 00:10:45.520
that, we’ll have to take another look at
the corpses.

00:10:45.520 --> 00:10:49.850
Let’s take a look at some of these bodies,
and try to make some connections. We already

00:10:49.850 --> 00:10:56.580
discussed the similarities between the coffin
and SCP-076, Able, the entity who also rests

00:10:56.580 --> 00:11:01.710
inside a large black coffin. Next, we have
a corpse dressed in yellow, with a burlap

00:11:01.710 --> 00:11:07.180
sack covering its head, tightened in place
with a noose. And removing it causes another

00:11:07.180 --> 00:11:14.510
sack and another noose to appear under it.
If you ask us, that sounds a lot like SCP-701,

00:11:14.510 --> 00:11:18.960
the Hanged King’s Tragedy, which revolves
around a play that heralds the arrival of

00:11:18.960 --> 00:11:25.029
a mysterious entity that calls itself the
Hanged King, a being with connections to the

00:11:25.029 --> 00:11:32.880
extra-dimensional realm of Alagadda. The Hanged
King entity in SCP-701 revels in decadence

00:11:32.880 --> 00:11:38.490
and chaos, so maybe it’s better for it to
be thrown into SCP-5555.

00:11:38.490 --> 00:11:44.310
Next, we have the corpse that’s been altered
with mechanical gears. That certainly sounds

00:11:44.310 --> 00:11:51.410
familiar too. SCP-217 is a virus that turns
the body into a clockwork being, replacing

00:11:51.410 --> 00:11:56.700
organs and tissue with the appearance of gears
and metal. Foundation researchers even noted

00:11:56.700 --> 00:12:02.089
the similarity between the body and the appearance
of a corpse fully transformed by SCP-217.

00:12:02.089 --> 00:12:08.420
But there’s also the connection to Dr. Charles
Gears, the famed researcher who acts as cold

00:12:08.420 --> 00:12:13.770
as ice, and frequently researches anomalies
with connections to the Mekhanite religion

00:12:13.770 --> 00:12:19.390
and the Church of the Broken God. It’s been
long rumored that Gears’ body is also altered,

00:12:19.390 --> 00:12:24.110
taking on the appearance of clockwork. There’s
no telling what this connection means, but

00:12:24.110 --> 00:12:29.440
it’s definitely something to think about.
Next in our retrospective, we have a white

00:12:29.440 --> 00:12:35.340
woman whose eyes were gouged out. While this
doesn’t exactly narrow anything down, the

00:12:35.340 --> 00:12:39.860
corpse’s secondary anomalous properties
certainly do. Photographs of the body show

00:12:39.860 --> 00:12:46.620
a pair of blue eyes that, when viewed through
video, follow the camera. A girl and a camera?

00:12:46.620 --> 00:12:54.029
That sounds a lot like SCP-105, the photographer
formerly known as Iris Thompson, who can manipulate

00:12:54.029 --> 00:12:59.330
the images in the photographs she takes on
her camera. Iris is typically one of the friendlier,

00:12:59.330 --> 00:13:05.680
more approachable anomalies housed by the
Foundation, and seeing her like this is heartbreaking.

00:13:05.680 --> 00:13:11.580
So if the corpses in the pit are former SCPs
themselves, and existing objects are reincarnated

00:13:11.580 --> 00:13:17.399
and modified after being placed there, how
many times has this happened over the years?

00:13:17.399 --> 00:13:22.970
Hidden files display test results involving
numerous ultra-famous anomalies, including

00:13:22.970 --> 00:13:29.580
SCP-173, which reappeared in an art exhibit
before it was contained again, but Foundation

00:13:29.580 --> 00:13:34.820
researchers were shocked to find that this
time, the statue was made of concrete, giving

00:13:34.820 --> 00:13:40.731
it the appearance we all know today. Another
test example involves SCP-049, the Plague

00:13:40.731 --> 00:13:46.050
Doctor, who was lured into the pit using a
vial of liquid that he was convinced contained

00:13:46.050 --> 00:13:52.760
a vital component to his medical mission.
SCP-049 reappeared in France, this time wearing

00:13:52.760 --> 00:13:57.680
the familiar plague doctor mask over his apparent
previous attire, a gas mask.

00:13:57.680 --> 00:14:02.430
There had been mentions of some sort of game
being played by the Foundation Administrator

00:14:02.430 --> 00:14:07.560
and the heads of various Groups of Interests,
involving a number of anomalies and the killing

00:14:07.560 --> 00:14:14.769
and recreation of different SCPs - Many turning
into those that exist within the SCP Archive.

00:14:14.769 --> 00:14:19.590
After Dr. Everett Mann’s encounter with
Dr. Holly Wondertainment, an email to Fritz

00:14:19.590 --> 00:14:24.250
from the Head of the Global Occult Coalition
congratulated the Administrator for an exciting

00:14:24.250 --> 00:14:30.080
addition to the game in the form of Dr. Mann
tracking the GOI’s leaders.

00:14:30.080 --> 00:14:34.810
Some, such as the leader of the Church of
the Broken God, contacted Fritz to express

00:14:34.810 --> 00:14:39.880
their displeasure at including the risk of
being murdered by Mann. They claimed that

00:14:39.880 --> 00:14:45.779
introducing such a rogue element to the game
after Fritz had already won felt like an indulgent

00:14:45.779 --> 00:14:50.620
victory lap. In addition, one reported that
Holly Wondertainment had proclaimed dying

00:14:50.620 --> 00:14:55.641
to be ‘unpleasant’ when she had woken
up after Mann had seemingly killed her. In

00:14:55.641 --> 00:15:01.300
trying to uncover the truth about this sinister
game, Mann had found himself an unwilling

00:15:01.300 --> 00:15:04.890
participant.
It appeared that the Administrator and the

00:15:04.890 --> 00:15:10.290
GOI leaders were immortal, and while they
could be temporarily killed like Dr Wondertainment,

00:15:10.290 --> 00:15:15.450
it wasn’t exactly an enjoyable experience.
Some GOI leaders even theorized that Fritz

00:15:15.450 --> 00:15:21.520
introduced Mann to their game as a way of
eliminating them or their organizations. However,

00:15:21.520 --> 00:15:27.670
Mann had no desire to kill any of them, apart
from Fritz himself, the leader of the entire

00:15:27.670 --> 00:15:34.850
game. In his notes, Mann urges his O5-1 successor
to share the SCP-5555 file with the other

00:15:34.850 --> 00:15:40.649
members of the O5 Council, to spread awareness
of the danger that Fritz, his various conspirators,

00:15:40.649 --> 00:15:45.730
and their game poses.
Traveling to England, Mann attempted to obtain

00:15:45.730 --> 00:15:51.160
Fritz’s location from Robert Bumaro, High
Priest of the Church of the Broken God. However,

00:15:51.160 --> 00:15:56.650
he found himself trapped by Bumaro and Herman
Fuller, head of another Group of Interest,

00:15:56.650 --> 00:16:02.130
the Anomalous Circus. Fuller knew that Mann
had worked alongside Fritz for years, and

00:16:02.130 --> 00:16:07.030
could prove useful for the next round of the
game, while Bumaro told him to simply kill

00:16:07.030 --> 00:16:12.300
Dr Mann, stating he “wasn’t worth dying
again”. However, Fritz appeared shortly

00:16:12.300 --> 00:16:17.589
after to take Mann into custody, threatening
to kill his associates Bumaro and Fuller if

00:16:17.589 --> 00:16:22.510
they didn’t release Dr Mann. While Bumaro
appeared more afraid of the dying process,

00:16:22.510 --> 00:16:27.120
Fuller refused to relent, resulting in an
exchange of gunfire.

00:16:27.120 --> 00:16:32.310
Fritz dragged the injured Mann away, patched
up his wounds and left him in a safehouse

00:16:32.310 --> 00:16:38.540
with clean clothes, bathroom facilities and
a note explaining what had happened. Fritz’s

00:16:38.540 --> 00:16:43.450
note told Mann that he’d left him a plane
ticket to Toronto, encouraging him to travel

00:16:43.450 --> 00:16:50.290
there and take out The Critic, head of Are
We Cool Yet?, one of Fritz’s fellow conspirators.

00:16:50.290 --> 00:16:56.570
The Administrator also left another updated
version of the SCP-5555 file, this time detailing

00:16:56.570 --> 00:17:02.000
not SCPs that had been replaced, but members
of Foundation Staff.

00:17:02.000 --> 00:17:10.029
It also stated that O5-2 to O5-13 were all
dead at Fritz’s hand, leaving only Dr Mann,

00:17:10.029 --> 00:17:16.259
O5-1, as Fritz felt they’d “bonded.”
Reassuring the other leaders that he wasn’t

00:17:16.259 --> 00:17:21.259
acting against them, Fritz explained through
emails that he had shaped Mann into the perfect

00:17:21.259 --> 00:17:26.319
element for their game. Mann departed for
Toronto, assaulting The Critic in an effort

00:17:26.319 --> 00:17:32.200
to gain more information, while also simultaneously
carrying out Fritz’s wishes. Dr Everett

00:17:32.200 --> 00:17:36.799
Mann, for his part, continued to carry out
Fritz’s dirty work, tracking the various

00:17:36.799 --> 00:17:43.210
GOI leaders and replaced Foundation Staff,
determined to topple Fritz and his game once

00:17:43.210 --> 00:17:46.279
and for all.
Come the start of the new game, Fritz and

00:17:46.279 --> 00:17:51.259
all his associates had switched roles with
each other. The Administrator of the Foundation

00:17:51.259 --> 00:17:56.679
took on the role of Dr. Wondertainment. Dr.
Wondertainment became the Prophet of Mekhane,

00:17:56.679 --> 00:18:01.950
a representative of the Church of the Broken
God. The role of the Global Occult Coalition’s

00:18:01.950 --> 00:18:07.640
D. C. al Fine became Jude Kriyot, a member
of the mischievous “Gamers Against Weed”

00:18:07.640 --> 00:18:14.169
group of interest. This new iteration of the
game also assigned Dr Mann the role of “Nobody.”

00:18:14.169 --> 00:18:19.080
His win conditions for the game were to kill
all the others, having himself been made one

00:18:19.080 --> 00:18:25.190
of them – an immortal – by Fritz. Assembling
his notes for the future O5 Council, Mann

00:18:25.190 --> 00:18:30.630
set out on his hunt for Fritz, carrying with
him a relentless grudge and signing off with

00:18:30.630 --> 00:18:38.960
a single item on a to-do list: “Kill Fritz.”
The story of SCP-5555, and the ongoing game

00:18:38.960 --> 00:18:45.100
that it relates to perhaps explains why we
bury our dead. Sometimes uncovering them can

00:18:45.100 --> 00:18:51.440
reveal secrets that should never see the light
of day. Some secrets, much like the dead,

00:18:51.440 --> 00:18:56.779
are best left buried.
Next, why not check out “SCP - 087 - The

00:18:56.779 --> 00:19:02.440
Stairwell” and “SCP - 096 - The Shy Guy”
for more anomalous tellings and explanations

00:19:02.440 --> 00:19:04.650
of the SCP Foundation from SCP Explained!

